---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Badge } from '@highjack/ui';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Rules — HighJack"
  description="How HighJack rules work: configurable rule modules, validation of impossible rulesets, and victory conditions. Full rulebook arrives with gameplay milestones."
>
  <header class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="m-0 font-display text-3xl font-extrabold sm:text-4xl">Rules, your table's way</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 mb-0 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      HighJack doesn't ship one rulebook — it ships a ruleset format. A match is defined by its
      <strong class="text-cream-100">GameConfig</strong>, and the engine enforces exactly what it
      says. Here are the principles that hold for every configuration.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <h2 id="principles-title" class="m-0 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">Principles</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-lg font-bold text-gold-400">The config is law</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Whatever the match configuration enables is legal; everything else simply does not exist
          at that table. Disable auctions and no auction will ever start; enable poker and Thursday
          night gets expensive.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-lg font-bold text-gold-400">
          Impossible rules are rejected
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Validation happens in layers: malformed documents are refused outright, structural
          mistakes (bad ranges, wrong types) are reported field-by-field, and semantically
          impossible combinations — like poker without gambling — never reach a lobby.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-lg font-bold text-gold-400">Money is exact</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          All currency is integer-valued. Chips can't be split into fractions, so arithmetic is
          always exact and identical on every client and server — no floating-point fortunes.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-6 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-lg font-bold text-gold-400">Luck is seeded, not sneaky</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Shuffles, rolls, and event draws come from a deterministic random stream derived from the
          match seed. The same seed and the same actions always produce the same match — which makes
          outcomes auditable after the fact.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="victory-title">
    <h2 id="victory-title" class="m-0 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">Victory conditions</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 mb-5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      Every configuration picks exactly one way to win:
    </p>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <article
        class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-5 text-center shadow-card"
      >
        <Badge tone="gold">last_standing</Badge>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          Outlive everyone. Bankruptcies thin the table until one player holds on.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-5 text-center shadow-card"
      >
        <Badge tone="gold">target_wealth</Badge>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          First to cross the wealth line you set — sprint or siege, your call.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-5 text-center shadow-card"
      >
        <Badge tone="gold">round_limit</Badge>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
          When the round limit hits, richest player takes it. No sudden death, just bookkeeping.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-felt-900/60 p-6"
    aria-label="Rulebook status"
  >
    <h2 class="m-0 flex items-center gap-3 font-display text-lg font-bold text-cream-100">
      Full rulebook
      <Badge tone="neutral">Coming with v0.2</Badge>
    </h2>
    <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      Detailed turn structure, property economics, and per-system rules arrive alongside playable
      milestones. We document what exists — not what we hope to build.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
